hexdump - display bytes as hexadecimal and text

SYNOPSIS
    hexdump [-C] [file]

DESCRIPTION
    Print the byte offset, 16 hexadecimal bytes, and their printable
    ASCII equivalents. A dot stands for a byte outside printable ASCII.
    With no file or a file named -, use standard input.

EXAMPLES
    hexdump -C /bin/echo
